<title>KENYA: Kenya shilling firm vs dlr, holding strong.</title>
<headline>Kenya shilling firm vs dlr, holding strong.</headline>
<dateline>NAIROBI 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Kenyan shilling was firm on Monday against the dollar on continued inflows from abroad, commercial bank dealers said.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Kenya posted a shilling mean rate of 55.01 against the dollar compared to 55.08 on Friday. While against the pound, it was posted at a mean rate of 91.04 from 90.78.</p>
<p>The money market was liquid with overnight rates quoted between 8-11 percent unchanged.</p>
<p>--Wambui Chege, Nairobi Newsroom ++254-2 330-261</p>
